Simple. Don't run wizards like a combat wombat. Think your way through
the early game, not fight through it.

While I won't even try to propose a full protection racket scheme here,
some of the elements are certainly applicable to early wizards:

1) Get your AC down.

2) Use your pet as your primary defense.

3) Realize that you are not equipped to smack down everything like a
combat wombat. That means that running away, Elbereth, and ranged
weapons and spells are all your friends.

4) You have one of the best resistances (MR) to start. However you need
to work real hard to acquire the others, especially poison.

5) You have to find balance in leveling up. You have to balance HP
(which are always on the low side), PW (which is always on the high side
and very useful to you), and monster generation (which will consipre to
kill you).

In short, leveling up should be a plan, not an afterthought. Everything
that you kill should be a considered choice. Leave everything else to
the pet until you've acquired the skill set and equipment necessary to
defend yourself.

